{
  "about": "Survey eval: `survey(sites, goal)` on shops in several countries and kinds of goods (a product's price, a category's listing, a service's price), so that nothing is tuned to one market or site. A site counts as found when its navigator reached the goal, the page's URL or title contains one of the site's `expect` (case-insensitive), and the quoted text contains every one of `facts` (a currency sign: a price came back). Run with `aibrowse eval survey` (needs a Jev key). Prices and stock change; the facts ask only that some price is there. Surveys with `filters` narrow each listing reached with the shop's own filters; with `max_price`, a site counts only when the filters were set and every price quoted is within it. The compare surveys ask a price-comparison site for a product's page listing shops and their prices (\"the best price for X\"), in three countries.",
